		Description		"The block captures the data window of a sampled signal and computes the orthogonal components of the s"
		"ignal, i.e. amplitude and angle. The pre-defined filters include Fourier and Walsh functions. The free expression fi"
		"lters may also be used. Note: The type of data window affects only the Fourier filter."
		Help			"This block take the date as its input window of the sampled signal, and convert it into a single orthogonal "
		"output. The output values are direct and quadrature orthogonal components of signal at the present sampling instant."
		"\nThe options of the block include type and data window length of pre-defined filters and user-defined filters."
